# Cline rules -- blackjacko

## Boot order (read at session start, in this order)

1. `docs/instructions.md` -- the canonical rules file. It governs; what
   follows is only its operational summary.
2. `docs/ROADMAP.md` -- the working roadmap: milestones as gates with exit
   tests. The only doc describing future work in detail.
3. `docs/spec-0.2.md` -- design law (v0.2 + errata, verbatim). The spec's
   Godot-era engine references are superseded -- the target is TypeScript +
   Phaser, 2D graphics; everything else stands. When code and the spec
   disagree, the spec wins and the code is wrong; while the TS migration is
   pending, surface conflicts, never guess.
4. `docs/dev_log.md` -- the development log: session rulings, changelogs,
   supersessions. Evidence, not law; consult when provenance matters.
5. `docs/PROJECT_MAP.md` -- auto-generated map of every src/ module and
   function, with docstrings. Generated by the docstring auditor; never
   hand-edit it.

## Gates before you call any change done

1. `npm run check` exits 0 -- typecheck (tsc is the only type court; vitest
   strips types via esbuild), vitest, and the docstring audit (a clean pass
   writes `docs/PROJECT_MAP.md`).
2. Comment law on every src/ edit (audited by `scripts/projectmap.ts`):
   exactly 3 content lines in the module `/** */` block; exactly one
   `/** ... */` one-liner directly above every function, class, and method;
   no multi-line docstrings on functions; `constructor` exempt.
3. Core purity: `grep -rni phaser src/` returns nothing -- the core and the
   sim harness stay engine-free; Phaser is presentation, later, at the edges.

## Working agreements

- Small, scoped diffs; one concern per change. Nothing is committed and
  nothing is pushed without an explicit human go.
- Design ambiguities: ask, never assume (`docs/spec-0.2.md` is the canonical
  vision, updateable by the human at any time).
- Memory bank duty: update `docs/` at the end of every working session,
  whenever the human reports a milestone or ruling, and whenever the bank
  has drifted from reality.
- Sim runs are evidence: battery outputs land in `results/` with a verdicts
  file. The 20M-hand `npm run verify` battery is a deliberate act, never a
  gate; the gate is `npm run check` and the vitest smoke tests.
